  "articleBody": "Sealing your log home's interior can really bring out its beauty, but there are a few common pitfalls to watch out for that can quickly turn your project into a headache. One of the biggest no-nos is sealing over dirty or damp wood. You absolutely need to make sure your logs are spotless and completely dry before you even think about applying that sealer. Otherwise, you're just trapping dirt or moisture, which can lead to mold, mildew, or a finish that just won't adhere properly. Another mistake is using waxy cleaners on your sealed surfaces; these can dull the finish and make it look cloudy over time. And don't even get me started on doing partial touch-ups! Unless you're a seasoned pro, trying to touch up small areas can easily lead to a blotchy appearance or inconsistent sheen, which ruins the uniform look you're going for. Getting an even finish on a large log surface, especially if there are existing coatings, can be super tricky. If you're unsure about moisture levels, product compatibility, or achieving a smooth, even application, bringing in an expert like HH Remodeling can save you from these common mistakes and guarantee a beautiful, lasting seal.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
